00 Feet/South Lincoln County; Logan County; Washington County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.29c08583e0a27279baf7ded8e86fe2e42bf50b69.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.29c08583e0a27279baf7ded8e86fe2e42bf50b69.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued July 28 at 5:37PM MDT until July 28 at 7:45PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...Eastern Adams County in northeastern Colorado...\nSoutheastern Morgan County in northeastern Colorado...\nWest Central Washington County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 745 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\nRises in small streams and normally dry creeks.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 537 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated the heavy rain was due\nto thunderstorms. Minor flooding continues in the advisory area.\nBetween 1 and 2 inches of rain have fallen. Water will remain\nhigh in creeks over the next hour. Light rain will linger of the\nadvisory area.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nBrush, Twelve-Mile Corner, Adena, Shamrock, Adena School,\nWoodrow, Gary, Leader and Hoyt.","ends":"2026-07-28T19:45:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Adams, CO; Morgan, CO; Washington, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a3b2efe930f6f0c1917c8b0285e1f108dda15b21.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.a3b2efe930f6f0c1917c8b0285e1f108dda15b21.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-07-28T23:52:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 282352 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 552 PM MDT Tue Jul 28 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Scattered to numerous storms expected TODAY and TOMORROW over the region; Storms capable of heavy rain - A few severe storms today, Flash flooding possible. && .SHORT TERM /THROUGH WEDNESDAY/... Issued at 134 PM MDT Tue Jul 28 2026 As of early afternoon, numerous ",